name>Seltmann</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Liebscher</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Specificity assessment from fractionation experiments (SAFE): a novel method to evaluate microarray probe specificity based on hybridisation stringencies.</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><volume>31</volume><fpage>E1</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12527790</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004808-Vainrub2"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vainrub</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pettitt</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Coulomb blockage of hybridization in two-dimensional DNA arrays.</article-title><source>Phys Rev E Stat Nonlin Soft Matter Phys</source><volume>66</volume></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004808-Anthony1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anthony</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Schuitema</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Boender</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Klatser</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Effect of secondary structure on single nucleotide polymorphism detection with a porous microarray matrix; implications for probe selection.</article-title><source>Biotechniques</source><volume>34</volume><fpage>1082</fpage><lpage>1089</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12765035</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004808-Howell1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Howell</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name><name><surname>Jobs</surname>